    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0580" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg496"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Sir M. H Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your note of March 13, respecting certain suggestions for
                    carrying out the purposes of the second article of the Alaska convention.</p>
                <p>In reply permit me to say that the matter is now under consideration, and it is
                    hoped that a definite answer may be given you in a few days.</p>
                <p>Believe me, your excellency, very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
